{"id": "185632", "name": "התאמת פונקציות בשני משתנים לגרפים – x²−y², 2x²y+x, y²/x (באנגלית)", "defaultgrade": 1, "penalty": 0.1, "options": {"multiplicationsign": "dot", "complexno": "i", "matrixparens": "[", "inversetrig": "cos-1", "logicsymbol": "lang", "sqrtsign": true}, "nhints": 0, "questiontext": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px\"><p>Match between the functions and their graphs below.</p><p style=\"font-size:0.92em\">(Note that in the graphs below the axes origin is at the middle of the grey rectangle and the red arrow is the x axis )</p><div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;justify-content:center;gap:12px;margin-top:10px\"><div style=\"flex:0 1 260px;text-align:center\"><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-weight:bold;color:#4b1f6f;margin-bottom:4px\">Graph 1:</div><img src=\"data/185632/files/1.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"250\" height=\"253\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"></div><div style=\"flex:0 1 260px;text-align:center\"><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-weight:bold;color:#4b1f6f;margin-bottom:4px\">Graph 2:</div><img src=\"data/185632/files/2.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"250\" height=\"242\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"></div><div style=\"flex:0 1 260px;text-align:center\"><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-weight:bold;color:#4b1f6f;margin-bottom:4px\">Graph 3:</div><img src=\"data/185632/files/3.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"250\" height=\"247\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"></div></div></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:14px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><p>(Please answer with 1, 2 or 3)</p><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">\\(f_1(x,y)={{CT:0}}\\) &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Graph number: [[input:ans1]]</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ans1]]</div><div style=\"margin-top:10px\"></div><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">\\(f_2(x,y)={{CT:1}}\\) &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Graph number: [[input:ans2]]</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ans2]]</div><div style=\"margin-top:10px\"></div><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">\\(f_3(x,y)={{CT:2}}\\) &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Graph number: [[input:ans3]]</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ans3]]</div></div></div>", "generalfeedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:12px 16px;margin-bottom:12px\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Outline:</b> Instead of plotting, look for a feature that can be read off each formula and seen in one picture only: where the function is undefined (and blows up), where it vanishes, its sign, symmetry, and its behaviour along lines or rays.</div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 1 — What identifies each graph</b><br><p><b>Graph 1</b> is the graph of <span dir=\"ltr\">\\(x^2-y^2\\)</span>: it is a polynomial, defined and smooth everywhere: a saddle. Along the \\(x\\)-axis it is the parabola \\(z=x^2\\) (opening upwards) and along the \\(y\\)-axis the parabola \\(z=-y^2\\) (opening downwards).</p><p><b>Graph 2</b> is the graph of <span dir=\"ltr\">\\(2x^2y+x\\)</span>: it is a polynomial, defined and smooth everywhere, with no singular line; on the \\(x\\)-axis it is the straight line \\(z=x\\), for fixed \\(x\\) it is linear in \\(y\\), and \\(f(-x,-y)=-f(x,y)\\), so the graph is symmetric with respect to the origin. Unlike a saddle \\(x^2-y^2\\), it is not even in \\(x\\) or in \\(y\\): the surface is twisted.</p><p><b>Graph 3</b> is the graph of <span dir=\"ltr\">\\(\\frac{y^2}{x}\\)</span>: it is undefined on the line \\(x=0\\) (the \\(y\\)-axis); its sign is the sign of \\(x\\): the graph lies above the plane \\(z=0\\) for \\(x\\gt 0\\) and below it for \\(x\\lt 0\\), touches it along the \\(x\\)-axis (\\(y=0\\)), and is symmetric under \\(y\\mapsto -y\\).</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 2 — The matching</b><br>Each of your functions is one of the three above, so its graph number is read off from Step 1:<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\(f_1(x,y)={{CT:0}}\\ \\longrightarrow\\ \\text{Graph }{{CT:3}}\\)</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\(f_2(x,y)={{CT:1}}\\ \\longrightarrow\\ \\text{Graph }{{CT:4}}\\)</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\(f_3(x,y)={{CT:2}}\\ \\longrightarrow\\ \\text{Graph }{{CT:5}}\\)</p>Hence the answers are<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ f_1:\\ {{CT:3}},\\qquad f_2:\\ {{CT:4}},\\qquad f_3:\\ {{CT:5}} \\]</p></div></div>", "specificfeedback": "[[feedback:prt1]]<br>[[feedback:prt2]]<br>[[feedback:prt3]]<br><br>", "prtcorrect": "Correct answer, well done.", "prtpartiallycorrect": "Your answer is partially correct.", "prtincorrect": "Incorrect answer.", "inputs": [{"name": "ans1", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 5, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}, {"name": "ans2", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 5, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}, {"name": "ans3", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 5, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}], "prts": [{"name": "prt1", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "sol1", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt1-1-T", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">The first match is correct.</div>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt1-1-F", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">The first match is incorrect, {{CT:6}} is the correct graph</div>"}}]}, {"name": "prt2", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans2", "tans": "sol2", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt2-1-T", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">The second match is correct.</div>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt2-1-F", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">The second match is incorrect, {{CT:7}} is the correct graph</div>"}}]}, {"name": "prt3", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans3", "tans": "sol3", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt3-1-T", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">The third match is correct.</div>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt3-1-F", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">The third match is incorrect, {{CT:8}} is the correct graph</div>"}}]}], "qvnames": ["f1", "f2", "f3", "g1", "g2", "g3", "lst", "lst1", "sol1", "sol2", "sol3"], "nvariants": 6}